 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "San Francisco Bay braces for its highest tides in forty years. Why now?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "The National Weather Service has issued a coastal flood warning for the San Francisco and San Pablo Bay shorelines, through Thanksgiving. Water could rise up to two point eight feet above a normal high tide, it told CNN, peaking on Wednesday morning."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Two forces are stacking up. The year's highest king tides meet a Pacific storm on Tuesday and Wednesday, with up to three inches of rain and gusts near forty-five miles an hour, the weather service says. Local reports say El Niño has also raised sea levels."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "San Francisco's tide record dates from 1983, also an El Niño winter. Forecasters expect water close to it, but probably not above it. Mayor Daniel Lurie has urged residents to avoid travel unless absolutely essential."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will the 1983 tide record survive this week? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
